{
  "title": "92: al-Layl الليل",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nوَالَّيْلِ اِذَا يَغْشٰىۙ‏(1)\nWAL LAYLE EZAA YAGHSHAA.\nBy the Night when it spreadeth its evil!\nوَالنَّهَارِ اِذَا تَجَلّٰىۙ‏(2)\nWAN NAHAARE EZAA TAJALLAA.\nBy the Day when (the sun’s light) shines!\nوَمَا خَلَقَ الذَّكَرَ وَالْاُنْثٰٓىۙ‏(3)\nWA MAA KHALAQAZ ZAKARA WAL UNSAA.\nBy Him Who created the male and the female!\nاِنَّ سَعْيَكُمْ لَشَتّٰىؕ‏(4)\nINNA SA’YAKUM LA-SHATTAA.\nVerily your striving is (unto) diverse (ends)!\nفَاَمَّا مَنْ اَعْطٰى وَاتَّقٰىۙ‏(5)\nFA-AMMAA MAN A-A’TAA WAT TAQAA.\nThen as for him who giveth (alms) and guardeth (himself against evil)\nوَصَدَّقَ بِالْحُسْنٰىۙ‏(6)\nWA SADDAQA BIL-HUSNAA.\nAnd believeth in the Best (of all religions, Islam)\nفَسَنُيَسِّرُهٗ لِلْيُسْرٰىؕ‏(7)\nFASANOYASSEROHU LIL-YUSRAA.\nWe will smoothen for him then the path unto bliss\nوَاَمَّا مَنْۢ بَخِلَ وَاسْتَغْنٰىۙ‏(8)\nWA AMMAA MAM BAKHELA WAS TAGHNAA.\nAnd as for him who acted niggardly and deemeth himself free from need\nوَكَذَّبَ بِالْحُسْنٰىۙ‏(9)\nWA KAZZABA BIL-HUSNAA.\nAnd belieth the Best\nفَسَنُيَسِّرُهٗ لِلْعُسْرٰىؕ‏(10)\nFASANOYASSEROHU LIL-U’SRAA.\nWe will smoothen for him then the path unto affliction\nوَمَا يُغْنِىْ عَنْهُ مَالُهٗۤ اِذَا تَرَدّٰىؕ‏(11)\nWA MAA YUGHNEE A’NHO MAALOHU EZAA TARADDAA.\nAnd will avail him not his wealth when he perisheth\nاِنَّ عَلَيْنَا لَلْهُدٰىۖ‏(12)\nINNA A’LAYNAA LAL-HODAA.\nVerily on Us (dependeth) the guidance\nوَاِنَّ لَنَا لَلْاٰخِرَةَ وَالْاُوْلٰى‏(13)\nWA INNA LANAA LAL-AAKHERATA WAL OOLAA.\nAnd verily Ours is the Hereafter and the Beginning\nفَاَنْذَرْتُكُمْ نَارًا تَلَظّٰىۚ‏(14)\nFA-ANZARTOKUM NAARAN TALAZZAA.\nSo I warn you of the fire that flameth\nلَا يَصْلٰٮهَاۤ اِلَّا الْاَشْقَىۙ‏(15)\nLAA YASLAAHAA ILLAL ASHQAL.\nNone shall be cast into it but the most wretched (ones)\nالَّذِىْ كَذَّبَ وَتَوَلّٰىؕ‏(16)\nLAZEE KAZZABA WA TAWALLAA.\n(He) who belieth (the truth ) and turneth (his) back (unto it)\nوَسَيُجَنَّبُهَا الْاَتْقَىۙ‏(17)\nWA SAYOJANNABOHAL ATQAL.\nAnd far removed shall be from it, he who guardeth (himself) the most (from evil)\nالَّذِىْ يُؤْتِىْ مَالَهٗ يَتَزَكّٰىۚ‏(18)\nLAZEE YOATEE MAALAHU UATAZAKKAA.\n(He) who giveth away his wealth, to purify himself\nوَمَا لِاَحَدٍ عِنْدَهٗ مِنْ نِّعْمَةٍ تُجْزٰٓىۙ‏(19)\nWA MAA LE-AHADIN I’NDAHU MIN NEA’MATIN TUJZAA.\nAnd no one hath (done) unto Him any favour, that he should be recompensed\nاِلَّا ابْتِغَآءَ وَجْهِ رَبِّهِ الْاَعْلٰىۚ‏(20)\nILLAAB TEGHAAA-A WAJHE RABBEHIL A-A’LAA.\nSave the seeking of the pleasure of his Lord, the Most High\nوَلَسَوْفَ يَرْضٰى‏(21)\nWA LASAWFA YARZAA.\nAnd soon shall he be fully content",
  "merits": "There are 21 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Makkah. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that the reward of reciting this Surah is so much that the one who recites it will be pleased when he sees it in his Book of Deeds. His inspiration of good deeds (Tawfiq) will also increase.\nIf recited 15 times before sleeping, one will dream about what pleases him most. Reciting it in the Isha prayers carries the reward of completing a quarter of the Holy Qur’an and is guaranteed that the prayers are accepted."
